  <h2 id="money-check">Money check before you pay</h2>

  <p>
    Degrees matter for licensed careers, so an approved college is not optional for nursing, pharmacy, physiotherapy, dentistry or medicine. But college is a small part of career success.
  </p>

  <p>
    Our strongest suggestion: keep the course fee near a tenth of your family's total education budget, and treat spending above roughly a fifth as a caution that needs course-specific evidence. This does not apply to free YouTube lessons or low-priced courses on sites like Udemy or Coursera, and the same course sold as a university certificate can cost 30 to 100 times more, so look at free and cheap options first.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
