          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">An illustration, not a real fee. The rest of the budget should still pay for living costs, books, a laptop and internet, a short skill course, and a reserve for a second attempt or a bridge year.</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Add every year: tuition, hostel, clinical and lab fees, exams and uniforms.</li>
    <li>Spend above the benchmark only for a verified, hard-to-copy edge, such as clinical access, council approval and real placement medians.</li>
    <li>If you could repay a loan only because you upskilled after the degree, the loan was not the degree's doing. Avoid debt unless the credential is legally needed. This is general information, not financial advice; get loan terms in writing.</li>
  </ul>

